      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "General nutritional strategies to promote whole body protein retention, particularly with relation to exercise, have been largely based on adult research that does not consider the dynamic process of growth and often ignores scenarios commonly experienced by children (e.g., exercise in the heat). Therefore, the aim of the present review is to highlight the importance of post-exercise protein quantity and timing in active children, specifically with respect to the whole body protein turnover."},
